{
  "requirement": "Criterion code uses {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.read_source` for this operation.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.read_source.fn` says only that criterion code uses `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.read_source` for this operation. The signature and behavior live in `ValidationContext.read_source`, and its sibling requirements `read_source.behavior` and `read_source.inputs` carry the detailed obligations. Those obligations need no separate test here.\n\nThe one marked test is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]`. It calls `ValidationContext::read_source(&OutlineData) -> Result<D::NodeContent, D::Error>` directly, which is the API the requirement names. It has assertions for each of these cases:\n- Unmapped sources return a mapping error, record no dependency, and do not call the provider read.\n- A failed read returns the provider's error and records no dependency.\n- A successful read returns the contents and records exactly one `Dependency::Node` with the mapped node and the contents' fingerprint.\n- The dependency goes stale when the contents change, checked through `record.is_current`.\n\nThe `{impl}` references are `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'_, D>]/fn[read_source]`, which is the operation itself, and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[parse]`. I found no obligation that the test misses and no marking gap.",
